          "id": "blk_jw99g6t6pk",
          "type": "quote",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "quote": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "As with all rite of passage ceremonies, the goal is always to be in service to the greater community, not just human, but to all life. Rites of passage are not about fulfilling one’s unmet needs, but instead, to awaken one’s consciousness to act responsibly toward self, other, mystery, and the sacred. To help create the new story, longing to be told."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "attribution": "Betsy Perluss"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
